        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "(6) Notice of Recall and Reporting for Work – Notice of recall shall be mailed by registered mail to the employee's last address on the Company's records. It is the employee's responsibility to provide the Company with any address changes. The employee so notified must, within seven (7) days after such notice is mailed, report for an interview or advise the Company of his or her intentions with respect to such notice recall. Failure to report or advise the Company, as provided above, or failure to accept a job as offered in the department from which the employee was laid off shall result in his or her removal from the recall list and shall void such employee's seniority rights. Failure to accept a job as offered in any other department shall not alter his or her place on the preferred recall list, nor alter the employee's seniority rights.",
